"""The unit console: web pages and a JSON API for one tvlink unit. Usage: tvlink-console [--fleet] | tvlink-console test

Runs as the tvlink-console user (tvlink-console.service) on port 80. Until a password is set it is in claim mode: only
the claim page, which needs the one-time code on the TV's splash (also `sudo tvlink console claim`). Root only through
sudo, for the tvlink commands in /etc/sudoers.d/tvlink-console; nothing from a request reaches a shell.
Pages: a session cookie, and a CSRF token on every change. API (/api/*): an API token (Authorization: Bearer), or a
session plus the X-CSRF-Token header on changes. Sessions live in memory: a restart logs everyone out.
--fleet: the fleet console, on any Linux box (tvlink-fleet.service, port 8080 on loopback, behind its own tunnel). The
same pages for every unit, through each unit's API with its API token (and a Cloudflare Access service token); its
own password, claim code (/run/tvlink-fleet/claim) and units list (/var/lib/tvlink-fleet), fleet user only.
"""
